s/94/948de5597ce1e4ad93b6d3344b463694d2cf1780903ca30a916a784d672e4d7c.svg) and ![](images/fa/fa8945e1ccf216ac0b94b3ae625f4c284190630782a4c0c2e24f4a94ea520d40.svg) we have that ![](images/60/600957eb8a00416e73e77c1866e0c065b489f6d32faa3215f3cef167ad8fcc21.svg) is indeed a valid solution.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the solution to our original equation is ![](images/09/0981bec86ce7424eb7dabbaa3827cc7591360dc24997730f3773c002f72a673b.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "bbec5a32-ab56-51ba-8362-e120d00857da" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5712 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
